  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "There’s a quiet shift happening in AI that most people are missing",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "And once you see that clearly, a lot of assumptions about evaluation, safety, and even what “training” means start to break down",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Large language models operate in high-dimensional latent spaces that are , for all practical purposes, incomprehensible",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Instead of treating hidden states as dense, entangled vectors, SAEs decompose them into sparse activations—where only a small number of features are active at any given time",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "What makes this release notable is not just scale, but intent",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "That second step is where things become engineering",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The implication is subtle but important:",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "One of the more surprising findings is that feature coverage correlates strongly with benchmark performance redundancy (ρ ≈ 0",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "we think we are testing broadly",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The ability to recover 99% of classification performance with only 10% of data is not just an efficiency gain",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "What matters is not the volume of data, but whether it activates the right features",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "For someone building systems around local models, this is powerful",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "What Qwen-Scope really introduces is the idea that interpretability can function as an API layer",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "This abstraction layer is powerful because it:",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "safety filters are just feature masks",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "style transfer is feature blending",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "domain adaptation is feature injection",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "not all features are cleanly interpretable",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "For builders working with local models and constrained resources, this is especially relevant",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Qwen-Scope is not just another interpretability release",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "It’s a signal that the field is moving from *observing intelligence* to *interfacing with it*",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "What comes next is whether we treat those coordinates as:",
